WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.050
You’re back alongside.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.100
Getting him aboard is the hardest part.

3
00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:11.700
Approach slowly, heading into the wind or sea if you can, so you can stop next to him under control.

4
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.725
Go to neutral well before you reach him.

5
00:00:14.975 --> 00:00:17.300
Bring him aboard over the side.

6
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.350
Never at the stern.

7
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.875
Why not the stern, where the swim platform is?

8
00:00:23.875 --> 00:00:26.300
Because that’s where the propeller is.

9
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:29.675
And never back down on a person in the water.

10
00:00:29.925 --> 00:00:35.200
Use a boarding ladder, a sling, or a parbuckle rigged from a line or a net.

11
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:40.450
A cold, tired, frightened person can’t climb, so plan on lifting him.

12
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.275
And once he’s aboard, you’re not finished.

13
00:00:43.525 --> 00:00:47.450
Treat him for hypothermia and shock, and get medical help.

14
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.900
People have survived the water and died an hour later on deck.
